.SH NAME
RTCPeerConnectionIceErrorEvent.RTCPeerConnectionIceErrorEvent \-
RTCPeerConnectionIceErrorEvent: RTCPeerConnectionIceErrorEvent()
constructor
.SH SYNOPSIS
The \f[B]\f[CB]RTCPeerConnectionIceErrorEvent()\f[B]\f[R] constructor
creates a new \f[CR]RTCPeerConnectionIceErrorEvent\f[R] object with its
\f[CR]type\f[R] and other properties initialized as specified in the
parameters.
.PP
Note that you will not normally create an object of this type yourself.
.SH SYNTAX
.IP
.EX
new RTCPeerConnectionIceErrorEvent(type, options)
.EE
.SS Parameters
.TP
\f[B]type\f[R]
A string with the name of the event.
This is usually \f[CR]\(dqicecandidateerror\(dq\f[R].
.TP
\f[B]options\f[R]
An object that, \f[I]in addition to the properties defined in
\f[CI]Event()\f[I]\f[R], can have the following properties:
.RS
.TP
\f[B]address\f[R] \f[I](optional)\f[R]
A string indicating the local address used to communicate with the STUN
or TURN server.
This should be set to \f[CR]null\f[R] if the local IP address has not
yet been exposed as part of a local ICE candidate.
.TP
\f[B]errorCode\f[R]
A positive number providing the \c
.UR https://www.iana.org/assignments/stun-parameters/stun-parameters.xhtml#stun-parameters-6
STUN error code
.UE \c
\ returned by the STUN or TURN server.
If no host candidate can reach the server and the
\f[CR]iceGatheringState\f[R] is \f[CR]gathering\f[R], this should be set
to \f[CR]701\f[R].
.TP
\f[B]errorText\f[R] \f[I](optional)\f[R]
A string providing the STUN reason text returned by the STUN or TURN
server.
.TP
\f[B]port\f[R] \f[I](optional)\f[R]
A positive number indicating the local port used to communicate with the
STUN or TURN server.
This should be set to \f[CR]null\f[R] if the connection hasn\(cqt been
established (that is, if \f[CR]address\f[R] is \f[CR]null\f[R]).
.TP
\f[B]url\f[R] \f[I](optional)\f[R]
A string indicating the URL of the STUN or TURN server being used.
.RE
.SS Return value
A new \f[CR]RTCPeerConnectionIceErrorEvent\f[R] object.
